content.text:
Updated the umbrella spec in the isolated worktree.

It now clearly says:

- linked groups release together; other packages only release when selected;
- the first safe version requires a clean detached Git checkout;
- old publish/tag commands become preview-only during migration;
- local progress is stored outside the repo by default, with explicit paths for CI/custom use;
- source publishing and compiled-binary publishing are separate operations;
- binaries need an intent-bound artifact manifest with source commit and SHA-256 checks before privileged release execution.

I also changed its status from `accepted` to `draft`. That is deliberate: the old spec was too broad and its implementation details were no longer trustworthy after the P0 review. The next step is to draft and gate the narrower implementation specs before accepting any of them.

